[31m-### Segmentation — DeepLabV3+[m
[32m+[m[32mAt inference we keep detections above a confidence threshold of 0.30. This threshold was chosen from a sweep on the validation set (see the analysis section).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Segmentation: DeepLabV3+[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDeepLabV3+ predicts a class distribution for every pixel and produces the final mask by taking the argmax over classes. The backbone is ResNet-50, and the Atrous Spatial Pyramid Pooling (ASPP) module gathers context at several scales using dilated convolutions, which helps separate the body from the panels.[m
 [m
 | Component | Choice |[m
 |-----------|--------|[m
[31m-| Architecture | DeepLabV3+ |[m
[31m-| Encoder | ResNet-50 (via `segmentation_models_pytorch`) |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Architecture | DeepLabV3+ (via `segmentation_models_pytorch`) |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Backbone | ResNet-50 |[m
 | Classes | 3 (background, body, panels) |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Loss | multi class pixel wise cross entropy |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Optimizer | AdamW |[m
 | Training | 100 epochs, batch size 8, GPU |[m
[31m-| TTA | Horizontal flip TTA at inference (averages logits of original + flipped image) |[m
[31m-| Output | Per-image PNG label masks → converted to `.npz` → zipped for Codabench |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Test time augmentation | horizontal flip, averaging the logits of the original and flipped image |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Output | per image PNG masks, then converted to `.npz` and zipped for Codabench |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe ground truth RGB masks are converted to integer label masks (0, 1, 2) before training. The same encoding is used everywhere: training, inference, and evaluation.[m
